# W4-EXPAND-LIVE-1 D4: the developer Load adapter (key L; not the original's warehouse trade panel,
# UI.1 F2.2, OQ-547) driven in the real window on the RTX 4090. Sails to the coast, founds the
# warehouse through the real founding tool (opening_resume.script's proven click), unloads one hold
# so the warehouse holds real stock, then loads some of it back aboard and confirms the fact line
# and the ship's hold change by the actual transfer, not the raw request. Launch:
#   --ship-start data/maps/candidates/ship-start-v2/lan5-ship-a.json --seat 0 --speed 200
wait frames 20
wait fact cities == 0 within 60000
expect fact gold == 30000
pick-ship 1
expect fact selected == 1
lookw 257 134
wait frames 20
sail 257 134
wait fact latest == arrived within 600000
wait turns 3
expect fact ship.1.x == 257
expect fact ship.1.y == 134
# The real founding (opening_resume.script's proven click: the sim accepts this rotation).
lookw 255 138
wait frames 20
key f
hover-land 255 138
wait frames 10
wait fact found.coast == yes within 5000
wait fact found.sim == None within 5000
screenshot 1-founding-preview
click-land 255 138
wait fact latest == accepted within 10000
expect fact cities == 1
screenshot 2-founded
# Stock the warehouse: unload all of hold 0. Hold 0 starts at 50 t of goods 42 (wood), but founding
# already paid 12 t of it away (ship-opening-playtest.md step 3), so 38 t is what is left to unload
# here (ship-opening-playtest.md step 4 confirms the same 38 t for this exact manifest and click).
key u
expect fact mode == unload
wait fact request == 38 within 5000
key enter
wait fact latest == accepted within 10000
expect fact store.42 == 9728
expect fact ship.1.hold0 == 0
screenshot 3-stocked
# Load mode: a developer adapter. The default request is 1 t; [ ] and +/- move it the same as
# Unload's.
key l
expect fact mode == load
wait fact request == 1 within 5000
key plus
key plus
wait fact request == 3 within 5000
key enter
wait fact tracked >= 3 within 10000
wait fact latest == accepted within 10000
# 3 t requested, moved exactly 3 t (the warehouse holds 38 t, far more than enough).
expect fact latest_moved == 768
expect fact ship.1.hold0 == 768
expect fact store.42 == 8960
screenshot 4-loaded
# Tab visits every hold, not only an empty one: hold 1 already carries 10 t of food (the
# ship-start's original loadout), so Load keeps that hold's own goods (food) rather than switching
# to the warehouse's most-stocked good. The warehouse has no food yet (only the wood just unloaded
# and the tools founding paid in): the sim correctly refuses this one, cleanly, not a UI guess.
key tab
wait fact request == 3 within 5000
key enter
wait fact tracked >= 4 within 10000
wait fact latest == refused within 10000
expect fact latest_reason == StockShort
expect fact ship.1.hold1 == 2560
screenshot 5-load-refused-no-stock
# A refusal does not leave the mode (same as Unload's): still in Load. Esc cancels it, sending
# nothing.
expect fact mode == load
key esc
expect fact mode == select
quit
